#45058
"Village Square"
"This is the center of the village of Chiiron.  The marks of commerce are

evident in the hoof scars and wheel ruts upon the road-stones.  Firmly seated

in the intersection is a cylindrical stone @efountain@n, covered in a dark,

mossy overgrowth.  Contained in the fountain is a foul-smelling, effervescent

fluid, apparently a byproduct of the moss, sunlight and time.  On the side of

the fountain is a small @esign@n.  A small, wooden chapel is directly south of

here, where the occasional tolling of the town bell can be heard.  Garnie Lane

starts to the north, with Trader Road crossing here east to west.

"
