#45138
"In the Duck Pond"
"The sounds of the living pond surround you.  The croaks of frogs, the

quacks of ducks, the honks of geese, even the gentle buzz of the deer

flies.  Lily pads float by among the cattails while waterbugs jump back

and forth across the water creating tiny ripples which spread like

circles in all directions.  Through the mud to the north the shore is

accessable, and in all other directions the peaceful, yet noisy, duck

pond rests, waiting.

