is very large, with a majestic staircase spiraling up to the next floor. 

Large paintings hang on the walls, painted with great skill and detail by a

master artist.  Gold-colored sconces hold torches to light this large hall,

further sconces line the staircase, together penitrating even the shadowy

corners of the ceiling far above.  Open doorways lead to a large dining room

to the west and a fancy-looking sitting room to the east.  A wooden door leads

to a smaller, more modestly adorned room to the north.

